<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Gelgel</h1><p class="st-meta">1380 CE – 1686 CE (approx.) · capital Gelgel</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Balinese kingdom founded after Majapahit's conquest, whose 16th-century court shaped classical Balinese Hindu culture.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit's</a> conquest of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bedulu-kingdom">Bedulu Kingdom</a> in 1343, Javanese rulers of the Kepakisan line were installed at Samprangan. By the late 14th century the court moved to Gelgel, near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-klungkung">Klungkung</a> in southeast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, which became the island's royal centre.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalem-waturenggong">Dalem Waturenggong</a> in the 16th century Gelgel ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/blambangan-kingdom">Blambangan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumbawa">Sumbawa</a>. The Javanese priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dang-hyang-nirartha">Dang Hyang Nirartha</a>, who came to Bali in that era, reshaped Balinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a> and founded temples such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanah-lot">Tanah Lot</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pura-luhur-uluwatu">Uluwatu</a>. Many Javanese nobles and priests fled to Gelgel as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> spread in Java. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> sailors under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornelis-de-houtman">Cornelis de Houtman</a> visited in 1597.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 17th century Gelgel lost its overseas lands and faced revolts, including that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gusti-agung-maruti">Gusti Agung Maruti</a> around 1651. In 1686 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dewa-agung-jambe">Dewa Agung Jambe</a> moved the court to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-klungkung">Klungkung</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> divided into several kingdoms, among which Klungkung kept the senior title.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1380 CE – 1686 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.16%;width:6.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1380 CE – 1686 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gelgel</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dalem Ketut, Dalem Waturenggong, Dewa Agung Jambe</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Balinese Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Balinese, Old Javanese (court)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gelgel, Samprangan-Gelgel</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1533&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gelgel" aria-label="Kingdom of Gelgel on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7869 2497 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Gelgel lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8189 2753L8186 2752M8189 2753L8112 2721M8189 2753L8189 2753M8189 2753L8195 2749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8186 2752h0M8112 2721h0M8189 2753h0M8195 2749h0"/><path class="